 **Formulas:**
-*   **3D Gaussian Function:**
-    $$ G(x) = e^{-\frac{1}{2} (x-\mu)^T \Sigma^{-1} (x-\mu)} $$
-    where $\mu$ is the 3D position and $\Sigma$ is the 3D covariance matrix [S2].
-*   **2D Covariance Projection:** The 3D covariance $\Sigma$ is projected to 2D space using the view transformation matrix $W$ and the Jacobian $J$ of the affine approximation of the projective transform:
-    $$ \Sigma' = J W \Sigma W^T J^T $$
-    [S2]
-*   **Alpha Blending:** The final pixel color $C$ is computed by blending the Gaussians sorted by depth:
-    $$ C = \sum_{i \in N} c_i \alpha'_i \prod_{j=1}^{i-1} (1 - \alpha'_j) $$
-    where $c_i$ is the learned color, $\alpha'_i$ is the re-scaled opacity, and $N$ is the set of splats contributing to the pixel [S2].
