 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Sparse Views:** The method relies on selecting "neighboring" views. If the source views are too sparse or poorly aligned, the depth estimation module $\phi_{depth}$ may fail to produce accurate depth maps, leading to incorrect 3D positions [S2].
-*   **Human-Centric Bias:** The method is trained on large amounts of human data. Performance on non-human subjects or scenes with different geometric priors is not guaranteed and may degrade [S2].
-*   **No Fine-Tuning:** The method operates without fine-tuning. Consequently, it cannot adapt to specific lighting conditions or occlusions present in the target view that were not present in the training data [S2].
+- The method relies on the accuracy of the depth estimation module $\phi_{depth}$; errors in depth directly propagate to 3D position errors [S2].
